with a high profile release of zack  snyder's justice league fans are  wondering whether the newest dc film  release will get a sequel  especially since the director's cut  wraps up with a big old cliffhanger  so let's dig into the big question the  4-hour epic leaves us with will the  story continue  zack snyder's justice league ends with  what clearly seems to be a setup for a  sequel  after an escape lex luthor tells  deathstroke that batman is bruce wayne  batman has yet another dream about the  nightmare reality in which he  deathstroke the flash cyborg mira the  joker and an out evil superman  are traversing the earth after an  apocalypse upon waking from his  unsettling dream bruce is greeted by the  martian manhunter who had previously  been masquerading as general calvin  swanwick and even disguised himself as  superman's adopted mother martha to  speak to lois lane  manhunter reveals his true identity to  batman expresses his gratitude for  bringing the justice league together  and tells him that they'll speak again  to discuss what darkseid is going to do  next  if zack snyder's justice league had been  released in theaters as the one and only  version of the movie with no  joss whedon cuts and no campaign to make  the snyder cut a reality a sequel would  probably happen  if you followed the first two movies  this movie really kind of takes you  into a completely immersive scope and  scale  reviews for zack snyder's justice league  have been largely positive with critics  giving him a 73  approval rating on rotten tomatoes an  audience is handing it a 96  score the film is dominating the pop  culture conversation  basically if the movie had been released  under different circumstances warner  brothers would be silly not to green  light a sequel  but zack snyder's justice league is what  it is a director's cut of a movie that  already came out in a very different  form in 2017.  snyder himself has said that he ended  the movie on a cliffhanger simply  because that's what he would have done  originally  not because of future plans he told ign  i wanted to just release the movie  exactly as it was designed  and that is what that scene is really  indicative of snyder also explained that  he could have crafted an ending that  felt more definitive and didn't leave  things open-ended  but that didn't feel genuine or  satisfying he said it's in  genre to end these movies on a  cliffhanger that's kind of how they are  and i just felt like that's what i  wanted to do  so is snyder even interested in  directing and writing the sequel  the director's answer to that question  is likely to disappoint many fans even  as it offers a slight glimmer of hope  in january 2021 snyder said in an  interview with comic book debate that he  has no plans to continue on with the dc  eu in the future  but he admitted that he never thought  he'd really be in a position to release  his version of justice league in the  first place so there's a very small  chance things could change  look i never thought i'd be here doing  this i didn't think i'd be finishing  justice league  as far as what i did and my vision for  what i wanted to do with these  characters and the journey i wanted them  to go on  it's well known that i planned on more  movies five movies or something but i'm  busy  i've got a lot going on is it cool that  the fans have so much faith in the  trajectory  yes it's amazing and i couldn't be  happier and i'm excited for them to see  justice  league so they can really drink the  entire elixir of justice league but  would i continue  i have no plan to but like i said i  didn't think i'd be here so who knows  snyder broached the subject again at ign  fanfest in late february 2021 making it  seem as though he might be more amenable  to revisiting his justice league world  at some point when asked if he would  consider directing a sequel snyder said  that's very hypothetical i think that i  would say i would believe it when i see  it  and happy to cross that bridge when i  see it approaching uh anything is  possible clearly  of course the key decision makers when  it comes to whether there will be  another snyder directed justice league  are the executives at warner brothers  and dc entertainment which fall under  the parent company warner media all was  quiet on that front in the lead up to  the snyder cuts hbo max debut  then on monday march 22nd warner media  got candid about where things are going  from here  in short the media conglomerate  maintains that zack snyder's justice  league is the last dc movie he'll ever  make  ann sarnoff ceo of warner media studios  told variety that zack snyder's justice  league brings the director's trilogy to  an end  that trilogy is 2013's man of steel it's  2016 sequel batman vs superman dawn of  justice and now zack snyder's justice  league  when asked about the campaign to quote  restore the snyder verse and allow  snyder to create more movies in the dc  eu  startup said the snyder cuts is a one  and done situation and dc plans to move  forward with other plans  she said i appreciate that they love  zack's work and we are very thankful for  his many contributions to dc  we're just so happy that he could bring  his cut of the justice league to life  because that wasn't in the plan until  about a year ago  with that comes the completion of his  trilogy we're very happy we've done this  but we're very excited about the plans  we have for all the multi-dimensional dc  characters that are being developed  right now  so it seems that cliffhangers and band  campaigns aren't enough to make his  second zack snyder's justice league  happen  in the end at least one snyder cut got  to see the light of day  and that was a pretty unlikely  occurrence itself  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the dc eu are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you
 

